WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:01.527
<v Instructor>Okay, so let's talk about SAM.</v>

2
00:00:01.527 --> 00:00:04.910
SAM stands for Serverless Application Model.

3
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.220
It's a framework for developing

4
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.960
and deploying serverless applications

5
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.240
and all the code is in YAML.

6
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.840
So examples is that you can create lambda functions

7
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.900
using the SAM framework,

8
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.630
DynamoDB tables,

9
00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:16.920
API Gateway

10
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.110
and StepFunction's State Machines.

11
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.114
SAM can also help you to run Lambda, API Gateway

12
00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:23.850
and DynamoDB locally

13
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.960
making it super easy for you to create

14
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.430
a very good development cycle.

15
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.790
SAM can also leverage CodeDeploy when

16
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.820
you deploy new Lambda function versions

17
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.220
and leverages the traffic shifting feature.

18
00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.300
And that's something that is very important.

19
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.760
Also, SAM is using CloudFormation in the backend.

20
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.010
So SAM is a very handy tool when it comes to

21
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.340
developing and deploying serverless applications.

22
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.089
Okay, so what you need to know

23
00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:52.980
from as a pro perspective is the CICD Architecture for SAM.

24
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.520
So you would have a code pipeline to orchestrate everything.

25
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.670
Your code would be stored in CodeCommit.

26
00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.330
Then it would be sent to CodeBuild

27
00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.060
to build, test and package the code.

28
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.440
And then a CloudFormation step

29
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.360
in CodePipeline would be applied.

30
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.930
And the CloudFormation is relying

31
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:11.450
on the Serverless Application Model.

32
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.890
So SAM will also be there.

33
00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:14.830
That's a little square in the right example.

34
00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.730
And then because we are deploying a Lambda function

35
00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.480
then CodeDeploye will automatically be invoked

36
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.540
by SAM itself to do a traffic shifting

37
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.000
between your version one Lambda function

38
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.940
to your version two Lambda function.

39
00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.080
CloudFormation can also deploy your API Gateway

40
00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.110
and update it if necessary or DynamoDB.

41
00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.760
But this is just classic CloudFormation.

42
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:39.280
The one thing that you remember for SAM

43
00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.850
is that if it deploys a Lambda function

44
00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.890
internally is going to use CodeDeploy

45
00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.360
to perform this traffic shifting.

46
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.250
And that is very important to know this going into the exam.

47
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.083
And that's it.

48
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.990
Just a very short lecture about SAM.

49
00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:51.823
I hope you liked it.

50
00:01:51.823 --> 00:01:53.680
And I will see you in the next lecture.

